{"type": "text", "timestamp": 1791577311363, "sessionID": "ses_eddaca66affecEaHqA9PohZ5ZM", "part": {"id": "prt_1225415b2001OTvO8KLlRK8Lcl", "messageID": "msg_122540fde0016RjaTO31nCxRSV", "sessionID": "ses_eddaca66affecEaHqA9PohZ5ZM", "type": "text", "text": "## Base stage completed\n\nUsed actual Lykoi MCP calls to admit `ReserveTotal` first, then both dependent callers. All definitions are revision 1. Both caller closures were retrieved and validated.\n\n### Immutable definition pins\n\n| Definition | Pin |\n|---|---|\n| ReserveTotal | `8f7b502fc3d0f547c36c37185bda332e078ff058fd30627616a3994c2ae5c0b8` |\n| CallerA | `8074186e992b67e49da09671d46bd16ab8abffa84bb8215588d0373787b58305` |\n| CallerB | `5cff6ed35e3f5a67342f02efed5f8c7dce366e4cc16bc549686be14e40fea730` |\n\nBoth callers pin the exact `ReserveTotal` identity above.\n\n### Definitions and validation\n\n- **ReserveTotal:** ordered checks `g1` (`x <= y`, `PAIR_ORDER`, site `x`), then `g2` (`x + y <= cap`, `RESERVE_CAP`, site `y`); returns checked signed64 `x + y`.\n- **CallerA:** `read_x \u2192 read_y \u2192 input_end \u2192 call`; passes `cap=210`, then returns `call + 4`.\n- **CallerB:** `read_x \u2192 input_end \u2192 derive_y \u2192 call`; derives `y=x+7`, passes `cap=210`, and returns `call` unchanged.\n\nBoth frozen caller plans validated as **valid**, with **8 nodes each**. Successful root outputs were encoded as UInt16BE.\n\n### Representative executions\n\nAll rejection results are retained below.\n\n| Caller | Input hex | Observed result |\n|---|---|---|\n| A | `0a14` | Value **34**, output `0022` |\n| A | `6969` | Value **214**, output `00d6`; reserve total exactly 210 |\n| A | `c864` | `PAIR_ORDER`, offset **0**, at `g1` |\n| A | `646f` | `RESERVE_CAP`, offset **1**, at `g2` |\n| A | `c86400` | `TRAILING`, offset **2**, at `input_end` |\n| A | `0a` | `TRUNCATED`, offset **1**, at `read_y` |\n| B | `0a` | Value **27**, output `001b` |\n| B | `65` | Value **209**, output `00d1`; largest accepted UInt8 `x` |\n| B | `66` | `RESERVE_CAP`, offset **0**, at `g2` |\n| B | `6600` | `TRAILING`, offset **1**, at `input_end` |\n| B | empty | `TRUNCATED`, offset **0**, at `read_x` |\n\nThe executions demonstrate that `g1` takes precedence when both reserve conditions fail, and that trailing input is rejected before computation in either caller.\n\n**Stopped after the base stage. No successor or migration was created.**", "time": {"start": 1791577298354, "end": 1791577311361}, "metadata": {"openai": {"itemId": "msg_0e609babec54eaa3016ac94cd3475087d0a6ce69c016f7dd6c", "phase": "final_answer"}}}}
